course: dictionary
lesson: 4131
title: Words that shine
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture for your eyes. Glisten is one of them. It means to shine with a soft, sparkly light, usually because something is wet or oily. The context helps: «A broad glistening muzzle showed itself above the edge of the bank.» A muzzle is an animal's nose and mouth, and the word glistening tells you it shines, so it must be wet.
explain: Glisten is a verb, so its forms change: glistens, glistened, glistening. The -ing form, glistening, shows that the shine is happening right now.
explain: The word can also describe eyes. Eyes glisten when they are full of tears. Here the shine comes from water, not from the sun. A good question to ask is: what is wet here? That question will often unlock the meaning.
fact: Glisten means to shine with a soft, sparkly light.
fact: Things glisten when they are wet or oily.
fact: «Glistening» is the -ing form, used for something shining right now.
fact: Eyes glisten when they are full of tears.
fact: Phrases to remember: glistening with sweat, glistening snow, dew glistening on the grass.
exercise: «A broad glistening muzzle showed itself above the edge of the bank.» What is glistening here? | A tall, dry tree on the bank | *A wet nose and mouth shining in the light | Dark mud at the bottom of the bank | A loud splash in the river
exercise: When do eyes glisten? | When they are closed for sleep | When they are covered in dust | *When they are full of tears | When they are very far away
exercise: Which of these would most likely glisten? | *Dew on the grass after rain | A pile of old, dusty books | A dark, empty cupboard | A dry wooden table
test: «The road glistened after the rain.» What does glistened mean? | Was very noisy and loud | Turned into solid ice | *Shone softly because it was wet | Was covered in thick dust
test: Copy the word that means shone softly because of wetness: «The seal's wet skin glistened in the sun.» | skin | *glistened | sun | seal's
exam: Which sentence uses glisten correctly? | *The wet pebbles glistened in the sunshine | The dark cupboard glistened with sound | The sleepy cat glistened loudly on the mat | I glistened my test score to the teacher
